file: "packages/editor/src/shell/palette_search.ts"
doc: "Narrow and rank palette rows against what the user has typed."

methods: [
  { name: "filterPaletteItems"
    change_type: ADDED
    doc:
      "Pure. Case-insensitive substring match against PaletteItem.label only\n"
      "-- NOT against `detail`. Matching the detail column would let a query\n"
      "match a chord or the word 'node', surfacing rows whose visible text\n"
      "does not contain what was typed.\n"
      "\n"
      "TRIM THE QUERY FIRST, then apply everything below to the trimmed\n"
      "string. So a query of '' or '   ' returns every item in the order\n"
      "given, and 'node ' behaves exactly as 'node' -- a trailing space from\n"
      "a fast typist must not empty the list.\n"
      "\n"
      "RANKING, applied to the matching items only: rows whose label STARTS\n"
      "WITH the query come before rows that merely contain it. Within each of\n"
      "those two tiers the input order is preserved. So the result is stable\n"
      "-- the same items and query always give the same order -- and typing\n"
      "one more character never reorders two rows that both still match in\n"
      "the same tier.\n"
      "\n"
      "No fuzzy or subsequence matching. 'nd' does not match 'node'.\n"
      "\n"
      "This REVERSES docs/editor-ui-review.md 11.5, which specifies 'fuzzy\n"
      "search by name'. The reversal is deliberate and that doc is not being\n"
      "amended here: a subsequence matcher ranks by score, and a score that\n"
      "changes on every keystroke makes the highlighted row jump under a user\n"
      "who is still typing, which costs more than the looser matching gains.\n"
      "Revisit if substring matching proves too strict in use.\n"
      "\n"
      "Concretely, with labels ['Node A', 'Annotate', 'Auto-layout'] and\n"
      "query 'a': 'Annotate' and 'Auto-layout' rank above 'Node A', and\n"
      "'Annotate' stays ahead of 'Auto-layout' because it came first in."
    inputs: [
      { name: "items", type: { named: { symbol: "ReadonlyArray", args: [ { named: { symbol: "PaletteItem" } } ] } } },
      { name: "query", type: { primitive: CHARACTER } }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [ { named: { symbol: "PaletteItem" } } ] } }
  }
]
